@startuml
    !startsub WORLD
    package com.cropa.model.world {
        interface Occupant {
            +onCrossedBy(crosser : Damageable):boolean
            +onBittenByMole():boolean
            +spriteKey():String
            +onHarvested():OptionalInt
            +blocks(blocker : CropType):boolean
        }
        note bottom of Occupant
            What occupies a cell of the field: a crop, a scarecrow or a bramble.
            Nobody asks what the occupant is: it is told what happens, and it reacts in its own way.
            onCrossedBy: an enemy on foot crosses the cell; true -> the occupant leaves the cell (crushed crop).
            onBittenByMole: true -> eaten (a crop); false for the bramble and the scarecrow.
            spriteKey: the sprite key, never a file path (SpriteCatalog makes the link).
        end note
        interface Damageable {
            +takeDamage(amount : int):void
            +getHealth():int
        }
        note bottom of Damageable
            What can take a hit: the farm and the enemies.
            The attacker only knows this interface: a bramble hurts a witch without knowing it is a witch.
        end note
        interface Updatable {
            +update(delta : float):void
        }
        note bottom of Updatable
            What moves forward with time: the enemies, then the defenses.
        end note
        interface DefenseLine {
            +wearAt(row : int, column : int, percent : int):void
        }
        note bottom of DefenseLine
            What a fleeing enemy may do to the defenses: wear the one on its fleeing row.
            Row 0: top slots; row 4: bottom slots; any other row -> nothing.
            In model.world, not in model.defense: track B uses it without depending on track C
            (dependency inversion, like Damageable). DefenseSlots implements it.
        end note
        interface FieldView {
            +spriteAt(row : int, column : int):Optional<String>
        }
        note bottom of FieldView
            What the view may know about the field: the sprite of each cell, nothing more.
            WorldRenderer receives this type instead of Board: it reads the field, but cannot plant or remove.
            Empty Optional: the cell is free.
        end note
        class Board {
            +{static} ROWS : int
            +{static} COLUMNS : int
            +Board()
            +getCell(row : int, column : int):Cell
            +getCells():List<Cell>
            +getCrops():List<Crop>
            +spriteAt(row : int, column : int):Optional<String>
        }
        note bottom of Board
            The field: 15 cells, 3 rows x 5 columns.
            Rows 1 to 3, columns 1 to 5 (like r1c1 to r3c5 on the map).
            ROWS (3) and COLUMNS (5): public, the only copy of the board size (L5, D10); the view,
            the defenses and the enemies read them instead of writing 3 and 5.
            getCells: the 15 cells, from r1c1 to r3c5, in a new list (one single loop for everyone).
            getCell: outside the field -> IllegalArgumentException.
            getCrops: the crops placed on the field, without the defenses, in a new list on each call.
        end note
        class Cell {
            +Cell(row : int, column : int)
            +getRow():int
            +getColumn():int
            +getOccupant():Optional<Occupant>
            +isEmpty():boolean
            +place(occupant : Occupant):boolean
            +remove():void
            +crossBy(crosser : Damageable):void
        }
        note bottom of Cell
            A cell: its row, its column and at most one occupant.
            place: cell already occupied -> false, nothing is placed.
            remove frees the cell (harvest, eaten crop, destroyed defense).
            crossBy: notifies the occupant, and frees the cell if it answers that it leaves. Empty cell -> nothing.
        end note
        enum CropType {
            CARROT
            TURNIP
            GARLIC
            PUMPKIN
        }
        note bottom of CropType
            The 4 crops that can be sold. The bramble is a defense (track C),
            even if the player picks it in the "Planter" (Plant) menu.
        end note
        class Crop {
            +Crop(type : CropType, config : CropConfig)
            +getType():CropType
            +getStage():int
            +isMature():boolean
            +grow():void
            +getValue():int
            +onCrossedBy(crosser : Damageable):boolean
            +onBittenByMole():boolean
            +spriteKey():String
            +onHarvested():OptionalInt
            +blocks(blocker : CropType):boolean
        }
        note bottom of Crop
            A crop placed on a cell. Stage 0 when planted, ripe at the last stage.
            grow: one more stage at each dawn, nothing more once ripe.
            getValue: value of the stage reached (sold at once on harvest).
            onCrossedBy -> true (crushed), onBittenByMole -> true (eaten).
        end note
        class CropConfig {
            +CropConfig()
            +getSeedPrice(type : CropType):int
            +getStageCount(type : CropType):int
            +getValue(type : CropType, stage : int):int
        }
        note bottom of CropConfig
            Figures from §10: carrot 10 (sprout 5, ripe 40); turnip and garlic 20 (0, 25, 90);
            pumpkin 50 (0, 70, 210, 1,000 since the D10 rebalance, 800 on D9). Tuned in playtests without touching the logic.
            Stages from 0 to getStageCount - 1; getValue outside these stages -> IllegalArgumentException.
        end note
        Occupant <|.. Crop
        FieldView <|.. Board
        Damageable <|.. Farm
        Board *-- "15" Cell
        Cell o-- "0..1" Occupant
        Crop --> CropType
        Crop --> CropConfig
        class Farm {
            +Farm(health : int)
            +takeDamage(amount : int):void
            +getHealth():int
            +isDestroyed():boolean
        }
        note bottom of Farm
            150 HP (100 before D10), never repaired. 0 HP -> defeat.
        end note
    }
    !endsub
    !startsub ECONOMY
    package com.cropa.model.economy {
        class Wallet {
            +Wallet(startingMoney : int)
            +add(amount : int):void
            +spend(amount : int):boolean
            +canAfford(amount : int):boolean
            +getBalance():int
        }
        note bottom of Wallet
            spend: balance too low -> false, nothing is spent.
            The shop reads the answer before it places the defense.
            canAfford: spends nothing; the HUD uses it to grey out buttons that cost too much.
        end note
        class Shop {
            +Shop(wallet : Wallet, cropConfig : CropConfig, gameConfig : GameConfig, offers : List<DefenseOffer>)
            +getSeedPrice(type : CropType):int
            +buySeed(type : CropType, cell : Cell):boolean
            +sell(cell : Cell):boolean
            +getDefenseOffers():List<DefenseOffer>
            +buyDefense(offer : DefenseOffer, cell : Cell):boolean
            +buyDefense(offer : DefenseOffer, slot : DefenseSlot):boolean
            +upgrade(defense : Defense):boolean
            +buyUrn():boolean
        }
        note bottom of Shop
            Called only during the day: the view checks session.getCycle().canAct() first.
            getSeedPrice: price of the seed (CropConfig), to show it in the shop.
            buySeed: false if the balance is too low or the cell is occupied; nothing is paid or placed.
            sell: the harvest (sold at once); false if the cell has no crop;
            otherwise the value of the stage reached goes to the wallet and the cell is freed.
            buyDefense: balance checked, then offer.placeOn; paid only if the placement succeeds.
            The bramble is bought with buyDefense, even if the view shows it in the "Planter" menu.
            upgrade: false if canUpgrade -> false or the balance is too low.
            buyUrn: only takes the money (false if the balance is too low); the victory comes from GameSession.buyUrn.
            The defenses come from the track C items (DefenseOffer).
        end note
        Shop --> Wallet
    }
    !endsub
    !startsub GAME
    package com.cropa.model.game {
        class GameConfig {
            +GameConfig()
            +GameConfig(language : Language, firstGame : boolean)
            +GameConfig(cropConfig : CropConfig, enemyConfig : EnemyConfig, defenseConfig : DefenseConfig)
            +getLanguage():Language
            +getStartingMoney():int
            +getUrnPrice():int
            +getNightCount():int
            +getDayDuration():float
            +getNightDuration():float
            +getCropConfig():CropConfig
            +getEnemyConfig():EnemyConfig
            +getDefenseConfig():DefenseConfig
            +getNeighbourFacts():List<String>
            +getNeighbourLettersPerSecond():float
        }
        note bottom of GameConfig
            250 coins at the start (200 before D10), urn 10,000, 8 nights, day 60 s maximum, night 45 s maximum.
            Also holds the figures for crops, enemies and defenses: GameSession reads them all here,
            one single config per game. GameConfig() creates the three default ones; the second constructor
            lets a test give its own (balance tried without touching the game values).
            GameConfig(language, firstGame), called by CropaGame: the language of every text (getLanguage, read by
            GameScreen), and the neighbour's texts in it (getNeighbourFacts, from Texts): true at launch and after a change of
            language (neighbourFirstGame), false after "Rejouer" (Play again) (neighbourReplay).
            GameConfig() and the test constructor -> French, first game.
        end note
        enum GameResult {
            VICTORY
            DEFEAT_FARM_DESTROYED
            DEFEAT_URN_SOLD
        }
        note bottom of GameResult
            How the game ends: urn bought, farm at 0 HP,
            or urn sold at dawn after night 8 without 10,000 coins.
        end note
        interface GameListener <<Observer>> {
            +onMoneyChanged(balance : int):void
            +onFarmHealthChanged(health : int):void
            +onDayStarted(day : int):void
            +onNightStarted(night : int):void
            +onTimerChanged(secondsLeft : int):void
            +onGameOver(result : GameResult):void
        }
        note bottom of GameListener
            Observer pattern: the HUD implements GameListener and subscribes to the game.
            The model notifies its subscribers without knowing that a HUD exists.
            onGameOver: one single call, with the way the game ends.
            No event for Neighbour (D11): the view reads session.getNeighbour() every frame, like the enemies.
        end note
        interface PhaseState <<State>> {
            +enter(session : GameSession):void
            +update(session : GameSession, delta : float):void
            +canAct():boolean
            +isOver(session : GameSession):boolean
        }
        note bottom of PhaseState
            State pattern: the game delegates to the current state, with no if on the phase.
            canAct: buying, harvesting and upgrading are allowed during the day, forbidden at night.
            isOver: default method (false); true ends the phase before its timer.
        end note
        class DayState <<State>>
        note bottom of DayState
            enter: session.dawn() (crops grow one stage, defenses at dawn, remaining enemies flee),
            then getNeighbour().startIfToday(day number). update: getNeighbour().update(delta), her bubble is written.
            canAct -> true. End: timer at 0 or the "Lancer la nuit" (Start the night) button.
        end note
        class NightState <<State>>
        note bottom of NightState
            enter: Neighbour leaves (getNeighbour().leave(), even in the middle of a bubble), then the night's wave
            starts (WaveSpawner.startNight).
            update: adds to the game the enemies that the WaveSpawner spawns (session.addEnemy).
            canAct -> false. End: timer at 0 -> next day, or end of the game after night 8.
            isOver -> true when the whole wave has spawned (WaveSpawner.isFinished) and all enemies
            are dead or gone: dawn comes without waiting for the timer.
        end note
        class DayNightCycle {
            +DayNightCycle(config : GameConfig)
            +update(session : GameSession, delta : float):void
            +launchNight(session : GameSession):void
            +isNight():boolean
            +getNumber():int
            +getSecondsLeft():int
            +getTimeLeft():float
            +canAct():boolean
        }
        note bottom of DayNightCycle
            Keeps the current state, the day or night number (1 to 8) and the timer.
            canAct is delegated to the current state. update moves to the next phase when the timer is at 0 or if current.isOver(session).
        end note
        class GameSession {
            +GameSession(config : GameConfig, random : Random)
            +addListener(listener : GameListener):void
            +update(delta : float):void
            +addEnemy(enemy : Enemy):void
            +buyUrn():boolean
            ~dawn():void
            +getBoard():Board
            +getWallet():Wallet
            +getShop():Shop
            +getCycle():DayNightCycle
            ~getFarm():Farm
            +getFarmHealth():int
            +getCat():Cat
            +getFarmer():Farmer
            +getEnemies():List<Enemy>
            ~getWaveSpawner():WaveSpawner
            +getDefenseSlots():DefenseSlots
            +getNeighbour():Neighbour
            +getResult():Optional<GameResult>
            +isOver():boolean
        }
        note bottom of GameSession
            Entry point of the model: the view calls update(delta) every frame.
            Subject of the Observer pattern: notifies its GameListeners.
            update compares the phase, the balance and the farm HP with those of the previous frame;
            if one of them has changed, it notifies its GameListeners (neither Wallet, Farm nor DayNightCycle knows the HUD).
            getResult: empty Optional while the game goes on; isOver -> true as soon as there is a result.
            buyUrn: shop.buyUrn() paid -> VICTORY result; the next frame announces it (onGameOver). Called by the view, during the day.
            addEnemy: the only way to add an enemy (the NightState waves); the list stays private, nobody empties it from outside.
            The game starts on day 1 as in the rules: 250 coins, empty field, no defense (D10, Antonin:
            no more carrots or catapatate from the POC). Each night has its wave (WaveSpawner, started by NightState).
            Reads all its configs from GameConfig; random is the only source of randomness, given to each enemy.
            dawn (package, L7): the dawn, called by DayState.enter; DayState no longer imports Crop, Defense or Enemy.
            The neighbour's day is the first draw of random; the cat receives new Random(random.nextLong()).
        end note
        class Neighbour {
            +Neighbour(facts : List<String>, lettersPerSecond : float, nightCount : int, random : Random)
            +startIfToday(day : int):void
            +update(delta : float):void
            +nextBubble():void
            +leave():void
            +getCurrentBubble():String
            +isTalking():boolean
            +isBubbleWritten():boolean
            +isVisiting():boolean
            +getPhase():Phase
            +getWalkProgress():float
            +getDay():int
        }
        note bottom of Neighbour
            Her day is drawn at creation: 2 + random.nextInt(nightCount - 1), so from day 2 to day 8.
            startIfToday: called at each dawn; she comes only once, on her day. Her texts: GameConfig.getNeighbourFacts().
            update: writes the bubble at 20 letters/s (getNeighbourLettersPerSecond); the day timer keeps running.
            Phases: ABSENT, WANDERING (8 s in the forest), ARRIVING (6 s), TALKING, LEAVING (6 s), GONE.
            nextBubble ("Passer à la suite" (Move on) button): no effect while the bubble is being written; after the last one, she leaves.
            leave: at nightfall, no effect if she has not come (ABSENT).
            getCurrentBubble: the text already written, word by word; "" when she is silent.
        end note
        enum Phase {
            ABSENT
            WANDERING
            ARRIVING
            TALKING
            LEAVING
            GONE
        }
        note bottom of Phase
            Public enum declared in Neighbour (Neighbour.Phase): how far she is in her visit.
            The view reads it (getPhase) to choose the path and the direction of her walk.
        end note
        Neighbour +-- Phase
        PhaseState <|.. DayState
        PhaseState <|.. NightState
        DayNightCycle --> PhaseState
        GameSession *-- DayNightCycle
        GameSession *-- Neighbour
        GameSession o-- "*" GameListener
    }
    !endsub
    !startsub TEXT
    package com.cropa.text {
        enum Language {
            FRENCH
            ENGLISH
            +getCode():String
            +other():Language
            +{static} fromCode(code : String):Language
        }
        note bottom of Language
            The two languages of the game (after the project, for the portfolio). fromCode: "fr", "fr_FR" or
            "fr-FR" -> FRENCH, any other code or none -> ENGLISH; the desktop launcher gives the language of the
            computer, the web launcher the "lang" of the address ("?lang=en"), or else the language of the browser.
            other: the language button of the title screen.
        end note
        class Texts {
            +{static} of(language : Language):Texts
            +getLanguage():Language
            +number(amount : int):String
            +titleLines():List<String>
            +introLines():List<String>
            +status(money : int, farmHealth : int, night : boolean, number : int, secondsLeft : int):String
            +name(type : DefenseType):String
            +name(type : CropType):String
            +level(level : int):String
            +ending(result : GameResult):String
            +tutorialBubbles():List<List<String>>
            +neighbourFirstGame():List<String>
            +neighbourReplay():List<String>
        }
        note bottom of Texts
            Every word the player reads, in French and in English, side by side in each method (pick): the view
            asks Texts instead of writing its own words. One instance per language (of). Only the main methods are
            listed; the others follow the screens: title, cutscenes, HUD, shop, tutorial, Neighbour, end screen.
            French: the words of the game as the team wrote them. English: the same, with "Catapotato" and
            The neighbour's talk without its swear word. "3 450" in French, "3,450" in English (number).
            Only characters of the game font: no typographic apostrophe (TextWidth refuses it).
        end note
        Texts --> Language
    }
    !endsub
    !startsub ENEMY
    package com.cropa.model.enemy {
        enum EnemyType {
            MOLE
            BAT
            WITCH
        }
        interface EnemyView {
            +getRow():int
            +getCellsToFarm():float
            +spriteKey():String
            +isOnBoard():boolean
            +getHealth():int
        }
        note bottom of EnemyView
            What the view may read from an enemy: no takeDamage, no flee, no update.
            EnemyRenderer receives this type: the compiler forbids it to change the model.
            getHealth: read by EnemyRenderer to flash the hit enemy red (HitFlash).
        end note
        interface CellCrosser {
            +onEnterCell(cell : Cell):void
        }
        note bottom of CellCrosser
            What enters a cell. The shared code calls onEnterCell, and the enemy does what it knows how to do:
            no type check. Enemy implements it: the mole does nothing (it follows no row), the witch
            crushes the crop or wears the defense on the cell (Walker).
        end note
        interface Flyable {
            +onEnterCell(cell : Cell):void
        }
        note bottom of Flyable
            Empty default method: what flies triggers nothing on the cell.
        end note
        interface Walker {
            +onEnterCell(cell : Cell):void
        }
        note bottom of Walker
            Default method: cell.crossBy(this), the cell is the one that reacts.
        end note
        abstract class Enemy {
            #Enemy(type : EnemyType, row : int, config : EnemyConfig)
            #moveTowardsFarm(cells : float):void
            #moveTo(newRow : int, newCellsToFarm : float):void
            +getType():EnemyType
            +getHealth():int
            +getRow():int
            +getCellsToFarm():float
            +takeDamage(amount : int):void
            +isDead():boolean
            +isTargetable():boolean
            +isFlying():boolean
            +isOnBoard():boolean
            +getReward():int
            +collectReward():int
            +flee():void
            +hasFled():boolean
            {abstract} +spriteKey():String
            {abstract} +update(delta : float):void
        }
        note bottom of Enemy
            Row 1 to 3, otherwise IllegalArgumentException at creation. takeDamage: a negative amount is ignored.
            Comes in from the right and moves toward the farm, on the left:
            2 cells before the field, the 5 columns of the field, then 3 cells up to the farm.
            cellsToFarm: cells left up to the farm (10 on entry, field from 8 to 3, 0 in front of the farm).
            A defense attacks it without knowing its type: takeDamage, isTargetable.
            isFlying: false; the bat answers true, and the scarecrow does not hit what flies.
            In front of the farm: 1 hit on arrival, then 1 hit / 5 s,
            until it dies, the farm is destroyed or dawn comes (flee).
            hasFled: true once gone; the game then removes it from the enemy list.
            collectReward: the reward for a killed enemy, only once; 0 if it is still alive or if the reward is already taken.
            The board, the farm and the Random are given to it at creation (EnemyFactory).
        end note
        abstract class LaneEnemy {
            #LaneEnemy(type : EnemyType, row : int, farm : Farm, board : Board, config : EnemyConfig, moveStrategy : MoveStrategy, defenseLine : DefenseLine, random : Random)
            #LaneEnemy(type : EnemyType, row : int, farm : Farm, config : EnemyConfig, moveStrategy : MoveStrategy)
            +update(delta : float):void
            +spriteKey():String
        }
        note bottom of LaneEnemy
            The bat and the witch move in the same way: this code is written only once.
            update moves the enemy forward, asks its MoveStrategy for its row
            and calls onEnterCell on each new cell.
            spriteKey: the type in lower case ("bat", "witch"), followed by "_attack" for 0.3 s after each hit
            on the farm (D14, like Defense.isAttacking), or by "_back" while fleeing through a defense row (seen from behind);
            a new lane enemy only needs its three keys in SpriteCatalog.
        end note
        class Mole {
            +Mole(board : Board, config : EnemyConfig, random : Random)
            +isTargetable():boolean
            +isOnBoard():boolean
            +onEnterCell(cell : Cell):void
            +update(delta : float):void
            +spriteKey():String
        }
        note bottom of Mole
            Underground: targets a random crop, eats it in 3 s (visible: isTargetable -> true),
            waits 11 s, 2 meals at most (3 before D10). Does not eat the bramble. Ignores the farm.
            Extends Enemy and not LaneEnemy: it follows no row, onEnterCell does nothing.
            isOnBoard: only during a meal; underground, the view does not draw it. spriteKey -> "mole".
        end note
        class Bat {
            +Bat(row : int, farm : Farm, board : Board, config : EnemyConfig, defenseLine : DefenseLine, random : Random)
            +Bat(row : int, farm : Farm, config : EnemyConfig)
            +isFlying():boolean
        }
        note bottom of Bat
            Flies at 0.35 cell/s: triggers neither the bramble nor the scarecrow. Turns aside in front of garlic.
            Only wears (-10%) the defenses of the defense row it flees through.
        end note
        class Witch {
            +Witch(row : int, farm : Farm, board : Board, config : EnemyConfig, defenseLine : DefenseLine, random : Random)
            +Witch(row : int, farm : Farm, config : EnemyConfig)
        }
        note bottom of Witch
            Walks at 0.3 cell/s. Turns aside in front of turnip.
            Walker: onEnterCell crushes the crop on the cell, or wears the defense on it:
            -20% durability, not stacked (see the Defense note).
        end note
        interface MoveStrategy <<Strategy>> {
            +nextRow(row : int, column : int, board : Board, random : Random):int
        }
        class DeviateStrategy <<Strategy>> {
            +DeviateStrategy(blocker : CropType)
            +nextRow(row : int, column : int, board : Board, random : Random):int
        }
        note bottom of DeviateStrategy
            One single strategy for two enemies: blocker = TURNIP (witch) or GARLIC (bat).
            Cell ahead free -> same row; blocked -> free neighboring row, at random if both are free;
            none -> 0 (flees through the top defenses) or 4 (through the bottom ones), whichever is closest.
        end note
        class EnemyFactory <<Factory>> {
            +EnemyFactory(board : Board, farm : Farm, config : EnemyConfig, defenseLine : DefenseLine, random : Random)
            +create(type : EnemyType, row : int):Enemy
        }
        note bottom of EnemyFactory
            The only place that knows Mole, Bat and Witch. To add an enemy: a subclass,
            an EnemyType value, a case here, its numbers in WaveTable and EnemyConfig.
            defenseLine: given to the bat and the witch, which wear the defense of their fleeing row.
            Random always as the last parameter (team decision, D9).
        end note
        class SpawnEntry {
            +SpawnEntry(type : EnemyType, row : int, delay : float)
            +getType():EnemyType
            +getRow():int
            +getDelay():float
        }
        note bottom of SpawnEntry
            One enemy of a wave: its type, its row, and delay = seconds after the start of the wave.
        end note
        class WaveTable {
            +getWave(night : int):List<SpawnEntry>
            +getStartDelay():float
        }
        note bottom of WaveTable
            The make-up of each night (§10), from N1 (0 moles, 2 bats, 0 witches)
            to N8 (4, 12, 5; 8 moles before D10). Also serves as the wave config. The enemies of one type are spread over 10 s (D9).
            getStartDelay: 5 s, no enemy spawns before.
        end note
        class WaveSpawner {
            +WaveSpawner(table : WaveTable, factory : EnemyFactory)
            +startNight(night : int):void
            +update(delta : float):List<Enemy>
            +isFinished():boolean
        }
        note bottom of WaveSpawner
            Spawns the wave of a night. The wave starts getStartDelay() (5 s)
            after the start of the night; the delay of each SpawnEntry counts from there.
            update: returns the enemies spawned during this frame (empty list otherwise).
            isFinished: the whole wave has spawned.
        end note
        class EnemyConfig {
            -stats : Map<EnemyType, EnemyStats>
            +EnemyConfig()
            +getHealth(type : EnemyType):int
            +getSpeed(type : EnemyType):float
            +getFarmDamage(type : EnemyType):int
            +getReward(type : EnemyType):int
            +getDefenseWear(type : EnemyType):int
            +getFarmHitCooldown():float
            +getFirstFarmHitDelay():float
            +getSpawnCellsToFarm():float
            +getMoleMealDuration():float
            +getMoleWaitDuration():float
            +getMoleMaxMeals():int
            +getFarmHealth():int
            +getFarmerDamage():int
            +getFarmerCooldown():float
        }
        note bottom of EnemyConfig
            As a table (D10, Yohan): one private record EnemyStats(health, speed, farmDamage, reward, defenseWear)
            per enemy, in an EnumMap<EnemyType, EnemyStats> filled once by the constructor, one row
            per enemy as in §10. The 5 per-type getters read their row (getHealth -> stats.get(type).health()).
            Mole 5 HP, 0 damage, 20 coins; bat 20 HP, 0.35 cell/s, 10 damage, 30 coins, -10%;
            witch 45 HP, 0.3 cell/s, 20 damage, 80 coins, -20%. Farm 150 HP, pitchfork 4 damage.
            D9 rebalance (Axel's playtest): slower, more HP, stronger hits. D10 (simulated games): farm 150 (100), pitchfork 4 (5), 2 mole meals (3).
            getFarmHitCooldown: 5 s between two hits on the farm; getFirstFarmHitDelay: 0 s, the first hit lands on arrival;
            the same for the bat and the witch (the mole does not hit the farm).
            getSpawnCellsToFarm: 10 cells up to the farm when entering the row.
        end note
