    package com.cropa.view.gdx {
        class GameScreen {
            +GameScreen(session : GameSession, config : GameConfig, withTitle : boolean, onReplay : Runnable, onSwitchLanguage : Runnable)
            +show():void
            +render(delta : float):void
            +resize(width : int, height : int):void
            +dispose():void
        }
        note bottom of GameScreen
            The game screen. show: loads maps/map_v1.tmx (TmxMapLoader), the camera
            and a 560 x 320 FitViewport (35 x 20 tiles of 16 px).
            render: session.update(delta), then asks the renderers to draw, in this order: map and crops,
            farm, defenses, enemies, front trees (trees_front layer), free places in white
            (ShopWindow.highlightedZone), night veil, crop dots (GrowthRenderer), range of the open
            defense (shopWindow.shownDefense, OutlineRenderer.renderRange), HUD, shop, end screen, F1 outlines.
            Holds no drawing rule. While the title screen, then the intro cutscene, are shown:
            no session.update, and TitleScene, then Cinematic, instead of the HUD, the shop and the end screen.
            show: Texts.of(config.getLanguage()), given to every part that shows words.
            intro = Cinematic.intro(world, texts) with the title screen, an empty cutscene after "Rejouer";
            victory = Cinematic.victory(world, texts), drawn only if getResult() is VICTORY, before the end screen.
            Click: title screen shown -> on its language button, onSwitchLanguage at the start of the next frame
            (Gdx.app.postRunnable); anywhere else, it closes, nothing else; cutscene running -> next scene; game over (isOver) -> EndScene only: "Rejouer" -> onReplay at the start of the next frame
            (Gdx.app.postRunnable), "Quitter" (Quit) -> Gdx.app.exit(); while Neighbour talks, neighbourRenderer.handleClick takes all clicks;
            during the day, "Lancer la nuit" (hud.handleClick -> launchNight);
            then the shop (shopWindow.handleClick); then BoardLayout: slot -> handleSlotClick,
            cell -> handleCellClick; neither -> close. The shop decides (place, plant, open).
            resize updates the viewport; dispose frees the map, the canvas and the renderers.
            pause, resume and hide (required by Screen) stay empty.
            Neighbour (D12): drawn with the enemies, before the front trees that hide her in the forest; her dialog after the shop;
            every frame, hud.lockNight(session.getNeighbour().isVisiting()).
            Tutorial (D14, Antonin), in the first game only (withTitle): drawn after the shop; its click
            comes after the neighbour's and before the HUD's; while it is shown, session.update(0): the timer
            of day 1 stays full until "Commencer à jouer" (Start playing).
            Garry (D14): farmRenderer receives session.getFarmer() and getCycle().isNight().
        end note
        class GdxCanvas {
            +GdxCanvas(batch : SpriteBatch, camera : OrthographicCamera, map : TiledMap)
            +drawMap():void
            +drawSprite(spriteKey : String, area : Bounds, tint : Tint):void
            +drawText(text : String, x : float, y : float, style : TextStyle):void
            +drawLabel(text : String, centerX : float, y : float):void
            +drawCenteredText(text : String, centerX : float, y : float):void
            +drawNote(lines : List<String>, x : float, y : float, style : TextStyle):void
            +drawDialog(lines : List<String>, area : Bounds):void
            +drawOutline(area : Bounds, color : OutlineColor):void
            +drawNightVeil(area : Bounds, opacity : float):void
            +drawDot(area : Bounds, color : TextStyle):void
