            +drawFront():void
            +endFrame():void
            +dispose():void
        }
        note bottom of GdxCanvas
            The libGDX version of Canvas. Opens and closes the batch and the outline drawing by itself.
            drawText puts each text on a 75% black bubble, fitted to the text; TextStyle.GREYED: grey text.
            drawLabel does the same with a second font at half size, centered on x.
            Tint.HURT: setColor(1, 0.3, 0.3) for the time of one sprite; Tint.UPGRADED: setColor(0.4, 0.6, 1).
            drawNightVeil: the bubble pixel, stretched and tinted night blue. drawDot: the same pixel, in the color
            of the style (red, orange, green). drawRangeVeil: the same pixel, white at 35%.
            drawDialog: a dark bubble over the whole area, then the lines in white in the HUD font (the neighbour's dialog).
            Tutorial (D14): Tint.GHOST, the image at 60% opacity; drawShade, the bubble pixel in black at 50%;
            drawArrow, a solid yellow arrow (ShapeRenderer in Filled mode).
            Loads each image once (key -> SpriteCatalog -> Texture) and frees them all in the same place.
        end note
