        note bottom of FarmRenderer
            Draws the farm, old Garry, the cat and the pickup at the places given by the map. Fixed sizes,
            computed once. The pickup has no point in the map: it is placed from the farm point,
            parked on the dirt path, before the barrier, facing the exit (west); its image is cut
            at both ends: a cypress on each end hides them.
            The farm flashes red for a short moment when its HP go down (HitFlash).
            Its image follows its HP (D14): intact above half of fullHealth (HP at the start of the game),
            half destroyed from half down to 1 HP, destroyed at 0.
            Garry (D14, Yohan): during the day, in his armchair; at night, standing, "farmer_" + farmer.getFacing() in lower case,
            followed by "_attack" if isAttacking. Same farmerArea for all his images: he does not grow taller when he stands up.
            The cat, read every frame: sitting, facing west when it flees (isFleeing), with the MEOW bubble during its meow (isMeowing).
        end note
        FarmRenderer *-- HitFlash
        class OutlineRenderer {
            +OutlineRenderer(layout : BoardLayout)
            +render(canvas : Canvas):void
            +renderFree(canvas : Canvas, zone : Zone, board : Board, slots : DefenseSlots):void
            +renderRange(canvas : Canvas, defense : Defense):void
        }
        note bottom of OutlineRenderer
            Debug view, F1 key: 15 cells in green, 10 slots in yellow.
            renderFree: the empty cells (FIELD) or the empty slots (SLOTS) in white.
            renderRange: a light white veil on each cell that the open defense reaches (defense.reaches),
            by day and by night (D10, Axel's request, like the range of a spell in a tactics game).
        end note
        class BoardLayout {
            +BoardLayout(cellAreas : Map<String,Bounds>, slotAreas : Map<String,Bounds>, spotPoints : Map<String,Point>)
            +getCellBounds(row : int, column : int):Bounds
            +getSlotBounds(side : SlotSide, column : int):Bounds
            +getSpot(name : String):Point
            +toScreen(row : int, cellsToFarm : float):Point
            +findCell(x : float, y : float, board : Board):Optional<Cell>
            +findSlot(x : float, y : float, slots : DefenseSlots):Optional<DefenseSlot>
        }
        note bottom of BoardLayout
            Receives the places read by TiledLayoutReader: cells (r1c1 to r3c5), slots (top1 to top5, bottom1 to bottom5)
            and spots (farm, farmer, cat), and checks the 28 names. The only place that converts pixels to model cells, and back.
            toScreen: row (0 to 4, fleeing included) and cells left for an enemy (10 to 0) -> point on the screen.
            findCell / findSlot: empty Optional if the click lands outside the field or the slots.
            L5 (D10): no more ROWS / COLUMNS here; the view and the defenses read Board.ROWS and Board.COLUMNS.
        end note
        class Hud <<Observer>> {
            +Hud(worldTop : float, money : int, farmHealth : int, lastNight : int, urnPrice : int, texts : Texts)
            +onMoneyChanged(balance : int):void
            +onFarmHealthChanged(health : int):void
            +onDayStarted(day : int):void
            +onNightStarted(night : int):void
            +onTimerChanged(secondsLeft : int):void
            +onGameOver(result : GameResult):void
            +handleClick(x : float, y : float):boolean
            +lockNight(locked : boolean):void
            +getNightButton():Bounds
            +render(canvas : Canvas):void
        }
        note bottom of Hud
            Observer pattern: GameScreen subscribes it (session.addListener(hud)); it only shows what it is sent:
            money, farm HP, day or night number, timer.
            Second line: the "Lancer la nuit" button, during the day only; handleClick -> true if it is clicked,
            and GameScreen calls session.getCycle().launchNight(session).
            onGameOver: "Victoire !" (Victory!) or the defeat, in place of the button, which no longer responds.
            Red alert (ALERT): "Dernière nuit !" (Last night!) on night lastNight (D10: no more alert on day 9, the game is settled
            at its dawn); nothing more once the game is over. lastNight and urnPrice come from GameConfig.
            Urn gauge (D10), second line at x 180 while the game lasts: "Urne : 3 450 / 10 000" (Urn: 3,450 / 10,000),
            and below it a 136 px bar, green (drawDot, RIPE) in proportion to the money, full at the price.
            The day before (day lastNight): red "Lancer la dernière nuit" (Start the last night) button, wider, and below it a block
            of two small red lines (drawNote): "Vous ne pourrez plus rien vendre après." (You will not be able to sell anything after.),
            "Seule la défense de votre ferme comptera." (Only the defense of your farm will count.).
            Neighbour: her bubbles are drawn by NeighbourRenderer, which reads session.getNeighbour() every frame;
            the HUD greys out "Lancer la nuit" while she is there (lockNight).
        end note
        class ShopWindow {
            +{static} REMOVE_BUTTON : Bounds
            +{static} SELL_BUTTON : Bounds
            +{static} URN_BUTTON : Bounds
            +{static} plantLine(line : int):Bounds
            +{static} defenseLine(line : int):Bounds
            +ShopWindow(session : GameSession, urnPrice : int, crops : CropConfig, texts : Texts)
            +plantButton():Bounds
            +defenseButton():Bounds
            +upgradeButton():Bounds
            +openFor(defense : Defense):void
            +openFor(cell : Cell):void
            +close():void
            +isOpen():boolean
            +hasPendingChoice():boolean
            +getPendingOffer():Optional<DefenseOffer>
            +shownDefense():Optional<Defense>
            +highlightedZone():Optional<Zone>
            +handleClick(x : float, y : float):boolean
            +handleSlotClick(slot : DefenseSlot):void
            +handleCellClick(cell : Cell):void
            +showPlantList():void
            +showDefenseList():void
            +render(canvas : Canvas):void
        }
        note bottom of ShopWindow
            The shop on the screen, at the top right. Two fixed buttons: "Planter" and "Défenses".
            Each one unfolds its list (the 4 seeds; catapatate, scarecrow, bramble). The chosen line stays white,
            the others turn grey; a click on a cell (or a slot for the catapatate) buys and places, then the list
            folds back. Placement refused: nothing is paid, the choice stays (getPendingOffer for a defense).
            An empty cell also opens the "Planter" list: the clicked line is planted on that cell.
            "Planter" list (D14): "Carotte 10 -> 40" (Carrot 10 -> 40), seed price then ripe value (last stage in CropConfig).
            An empty slot opens the "Défenses" list (D14): the clicked catapatate is bought on that slot;
            scarecrow and bramble, placed on the field, are grey there.
            A crop: its panel, "Carotte, graine / en pousse / mûre" (Carrot, seed / growing / ripe) in the Growth color, and "Vendre" (Sell)
            (shop.sell, second click). A defense: "Améliorer" (Upgrade) (shop.upgrade), and during the day "Retirer", for 0 coins:
            on the field if onHarvested answers (bramble, scarecrow: shop.sell), and the catapatate opened from
            its slot (D14: DefenseSlot.remove). At the bottom right, during the day: the urn (session.buyUrn), always with its outline.
            highlightedZone: the zone whose free places are in white. Can be viewed at night: all grey, no purchase (canAct).
            shownDefense: the defense of the open panel, by day and by night (GameScreen veils its range).
            Too expensive (wallet.canAfford): line or "Améliorer" in grey, with no outline, and cannot be chosen;
            the urn keeps its outline, grey text, and the click buys nothing.
            showPlantList, showDefenseList (D14, Antonin): unfold a list without choosing anything, and leave it open
            if called again; the tutorial calls them, and so do the "Planter" and "Défenses" buttons.
            The words come from Texts; the outlines of "Planter", "Défenses" and "Améliorer" are sized from the words
            of the language (TextWidth): plantButton, defenseButton, upgradeButton.
        end note
        class DefenseRenderer {
            +DefenseRenderer(layout : BoardLayout, texts : Texts)
            +render(canvas : Canvas, slots : DefenseSlots, delta : float):void
            ~{static} slotSpriteArea(slotArea : Bounds):Bounds
        }
        note bottom of DefenseRenderer
            Draws the catapatates on their slot (throwing if isAttacking, D14), and the level and the
            durability of each defense (D14): on a slot, two stacked labels "N1" ("L1" in English) above "92%",
            on the side away from the field. Scarecrow and bramble: WorldRenderer already draws their sprite (spriteAt); here,
            only the "N1 92%" label above the cell, and the sprite drawn again with a tint for 0.2 s: red after a hit, blue after "Améliorer".
            The catapatate does not flash red (it wears with each shot); it flashes blue after "Améliorer".
            slotSpriteArea (D14): the place of a catapatate on its slot, centered; static and package-private,
            the tutorial puts its ghost catapatate there, at the exact place of a real one.
        end note
        class Tutorial {
            ~{static} AREA : Bounds
            +Tutorial(world : Bounds, layout : BoardLayout, shop : ShopWindow, shown : boolean, texts : Texts)
            +nextButton():Bounds
            +startButton():Bounds
            +isOver():boolean
            +render(canvas : Canvas):void
            +handleClick(x : float, y : float):boolean
        }
        note bottom of Tutorial
            The first-day tutorial (D14, Antonin; jury feedback: the player did not know what to do).
            Five bubbles: plant, defend (the catapatate), garlic, turnip, "Améliorer"; shown = withTitle,
            never after "Rejouer". Modal: handleClick takes all clicks while a bubble is shown,
            only its button moves on ("Suivant" (Next), then "Commencer à jouer" on the last one).
            render: the world darkened except the bubble's target (4 drawShade), the bubble in the neighbour's frame (drawDialog),
            an arrow on the target (drawArrow); bubble 5 places a ghost catapatate (Tint.GHOST), only drawn.
            Each bubble opens the shop list it talks about (showPlantList, showDefenseList) or closes it.
            The bubbles and the buttons come from Texts; each button ends at x 347, its outline sized from its words.
        end note
        Tutorial --> ShopWindow : opens its lists
        Tutorial ..> BoardLayout : reads at creation
        Tutorial ..> DefenseRenderer : slotSpriteArea
        class NeighbourRenderer {
            +NeighbourRenderer(layout : BoardLayout, texts : Texts)
            +nextButton():Bounds
            +renderNeighbour(canvas : Canvas, neighbour : Neighbour):void
            +renderDialog(canvas : Canvas, neighbour : Neighbour):void
            +handleClick(neighbour : Neighbour, x : float, y : float):boolean
            ~{static} directionOf(start : Point, end : Point):String
            ~{static} linesOf(text : String):List<String>
        }
        note bottom of NeighbourRenderer
            The neighbour's visit (D12), with no event: reads session.getNeighbour() every frame, like the enemies.
            Her paths are computed once from the farm point of the map: forest, gate, under Garry (seen from behind), dirt path.
            renderNeighbour: her place = path x getWalkProgress (0 to 1), her sprite facing the direction of the walk (8 directions),
            a small bubble on her left while she talks. renderDialog: the dark frame under the bottom fence (drawDialog,
            34 letters per line, 3 lines at most) and the "Passer à la suite" (Continue) button, grey while the bubble
            is being written, ending at x 343, its outline sized from its words.
            handleClick: true while she talks (the click is hers, wherever it lands); on the button, nextBubble.
            directionOf and linesOf: static and package-private so that NeighbourRendererTest checks the 8 directions and the line breaks of her real texts.
        end note
        class TextWidth {
            +{static} of(text : String):int
        }
        note bottom of TextWidth
            The width of a text in the game font (lsans-15, the default font of libGDX), from the advance of each
            letter and the kerning of each pair, copied from the font: the buttons are sized from their words without
            libGDX, and TextsLayoutTest checks that the words of both languages fit their place.
            A character the font does not have -> IllegalArgumentException.
        end note
