    !startsub VIEW_WORLD
    package com.cropa.view.world {
        class WorldRenderer {
            +WorldRenderer(layout : BoardLayout)
            +render(canvas : Canvas, field : FieldView):void
        }
        note bottom of WorldRenderer
            Track A. Draws the map (canvas.drawMap), then the sprite of each occupied cell,
            at its place (getCellBounds), with the key given by field.spriteAt. Knows neither libGDX nor Crop.
            The bramble and the scarecrow too, like a crop; DefenseRenderer only adds their durability and their tints.
        end note
    }
    !endsub
    !startsub VIEW_ENEMY
    package com.cropa.view.enemy {
        class EnemyRenderer {
            +EnemyRenderer(layout : BoardLayout)
            +render(canvas : Canvas, enemies : List<? extends EnemyView>, delta : float):void
        }
        note bottom of EnemyRenderer
            Track B. Draws each enemy still in play (isOnBoard) with its key (spriteKey), at toScreen(row, cellsToFarm).
            A hit enemy flashes red for a short moment (HitFlash on getHealth). One cell (16 px) per enemy,
            28 px for the witch (witch, witch_attack, witch_back), the size of old Garry.
            Knows neither libGDX nor the type of the enemy. Old Garry and the cat are not enemies: FarmRenderer
            draws them, with the farm.
        end note
    }
